# What the release binaries are built from: Hindsight's dependencies plus PyInstaller.
#
# requirements-build.txt is generated from this file and is what the build-binaries
# workflow installs, with --require-hashes. It pins every package, including the ones
# these pull in, to one version and lists the hashes of its files. requirements.txt
# keeps its ranges, and the tests go on installing from it, so a new release of a
# dependency is tested before it is built into a binary.
#
# To refresh it, after checking what changed in the new versions:
#
#   pip install uv
#   uv pip compile requirements-build.in --universal --generate-hashes \
#       --python-version 3.13 --output-file requirements-build.txt
#
# --universal writes one file for Windows, Linux and macOS, with a marker on each
# package only some of them need (pywin32, for one). Add --upgrade to move everything
# to its newest version, or --upgrade-package NAME for one package.
-r requirements.txt
pyinstaller
